"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/5181","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/5181.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-11T00:40:46Z"},"body":"Fixes #4071\n\n## Summary\n\n```text\nvalidate\n  reject inconsistent bounds, windows, fees, ledgers, rates, caps, and allowlists\nfold_authorisation\n  ignore invalid higher versions and retain the highest valid body\n```\n\n- Treat zero rate numerator, zero total cap, and an empty allowlist as invalid, consistent with the positive-rate and non-empty policy documentation.\n- Keep gateway checks (#3801), duplicate-version tie-breaking (#4069), and the separate signing-path concern (#4414) out of scope.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** current main checked issuer identity and nonzero denominator only; issue #4071 documents malformed bodies that passed validation and folded as live.\n- **After:** added per-shape validation tests and a regression test proving an invalid higher version does not shadow a prior valid body. The targeted local cargo test is rerunning after its first build exceeded the 10-minute shell limit; results will be recorded on the task.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** small — rejects malformed or non-actionable authorisations at the existing validation gate.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796335808&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=5181&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F5181&signature=463db334ae9097b0cb2d77a7df39e790ea61d410a4f924c951f60fd42b4f4958\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/5181?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/5181/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/5181/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8677","id":6329036619,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABOYSY2g","number":8677,"title":"fix(id): enforce validate() in sign_authorisation (#6422)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-11-11T13:02:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T01:25:15Z","closed_at":"2026-11-11T14:15:04Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8677","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8677","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8677.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8677.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-11T14:15:04Z"},"body":"Closes #6422.\n\n## What\n\n`sign_authorisation` (pkgs/id/src/currency.rs) never called `RateAuthorisation::validate`, so bodies the fold will always ignore — an authorisation naming another issuer, `rate_den = 0`, and every other validate rule — signed successfully and were dead on arrival.\n\nIt now validates the authorisation against the signing key's issuer (`issuer_id(key)`) before signing. Failures surface as a new `SignError::Validate(ValidateError)` variant (with `From<ValidateError>` and Display coverage), so callers can match the exact validation failure. `sign_revoke` is unchanged: no validate exists for revokes, and inventing one is out of scope, as is extending validate's rules (#4071).\n\n## Verification\n\n- New tests: `sign_authorisation_refuses_an_authorisation_for_another_issuer` (SignError::Validate(IssuerMismatch)) and `sign_authorisation_refuses_a_zero_rate_denominator` (SignError::Validate(ZeroRateDenominator)).\n- `cargo test -p id --lib currency` — pass (see task 10861 note on #6422); the existing `signed_events_round_trip_through_the_fold` covers the valid signing path.\n- No other callers of `sign_authorisation` exist in the repo (grep), so the new refusal has no downstream breakage.\n\nTask 10861 (lane any-b).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796994176&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8677&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8677&signature=12cb81e1f1d3423de96e6f126707f781a45ffa672a326a31f995787f525171a4\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8677?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8677/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2883","id":6129101616,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABL45jlw","number":2883,"title":"fix(mcpx): Clamp validates request against the dial's own enum first (#1641)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-31T00:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T16:03:35Z","closed_at":"2026-11-02T16:03:32Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/2883","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2883","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2883.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2883.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-02T16:03:32Z"},"body":"Fixes #1641.\n\n## Problem\n\n`Set.Clamp` (`pkgs/mcpx/internal/settings/clamp.go`) ranked the requested value only in the **ceiling's** enum (`cdecl.Rank`) — the dial's own `decl.Rank` was never consulted. Ceiling-ladder values outside a subset dial's enum passed as valid: `prompt.autonomy` (`{propose, run}`) accepted `apply`/`off`/`advise`/`ask` under the default ceiling, and the invalid-value error listed the ceiling's ladder instead of the dial's values.\n\n## Fix\n\nValidate `requested` against the dial's own enum first (error names the dial's values), then rank in the ceiling for the lowering comparison. The ceiling check stays as a defensive backstop (unreachable for `New`-validated schemas, where the dial enum must be an ordered subset of the ceiling enum).\n\nPinned lowering is preserved: a request above the ceiling still lowers to the ceiling value, including a ceiling below the dial's whole range.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Regression tests added on the existing subset-dial fixture in `clamp_test.go`: `off`/`advise`/`ask`/`apply` now error, name `[propose run]`, and never list the ceiling ladder.\n- `go test ./internal/settings/ -run 'TestNewRefusesAClampThatCannotHold|TestACallerCannotRaiseAClampedSetting'`: PASS (run locally in the task worktree).\n- Full package baseline-compare: clean `origin/main` (`b5d334b0`) fails the same 5 tests before and after this change (`TestEveryDocumentHasAChapter`, `TestNoUndeclaredEnvRead`, `TestEverySettingHasAnEffectProbeOrAnExemption`, `TestTheScriptEnvironmentIsWhatTheCodeSets`, `TestTheEnvironmentDocIsCurrent` — the pre-existing #2846 reds). No new failures; no clamp test fails.\n\n## Scope notes\n\n- `promptAutonomy` (`routes_consumer.go`) pre-validates to propose/run before calling `Clamp`, so its behavior is unchanged.\n- #2846 untouched, per the task packet.\n\n🤖 Agent note: queue task 4071 (repo-worker-code, openchamber scheduled lane).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2883/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13866","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13866/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13866/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/13866/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13866","id":6571270143,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRaM9iw","number":13866,"title":"feat(fleet): seat-time steward hard-stop registry for pool guards (#2732)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-23T23:48:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T02:05:11Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T00:11:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/13866","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13866","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13866.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/13866.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-24T00:11:57Z"},"body":"Next slice of #2732 (proposal step 2 — a steward hard-stop note recorded in a machine-readable place the seating paths check).\n\n## What this slice does\n`placement-record --hard-stops <hard-stops.json>` checks a steward-written stop registry for the seating's pool before evaluating:\n- a stop entry sets `pool_hard_stop` and refuses with the hard-stop line `placement-audit --log` already counts (`[source: hard-stop]`), even at 42% monthly;\n- absent entries and explicit `stopped: false` seat unaffected;\n- stops are sticky (the file adds, never clears) and a missing/malformed registry — or a missing pool identity — fails loudly instead of seating unguarded.\n\n## Evidence\n- `go test ./... -count=1` green in `pkgs/fleet/placement` (11 new tests: reader contract + seating-path behavior); `go vet` clean; treefmt clean.\n- End-to-end against the policy of record: stopped pool at 42% monthly refuses (exit 1) with the countable line; unstopped pool seats R6/Muse (exit 0).\n\n## Follow-up (not this slice)\n- The steward writer that maintains `hard-stops.json` beside `quota-current.json`.\n- The trailing-pace input (`pool_pace_pph`) still has no live producer — the pace guard cannot trigger in production yet.\n\n<!-- pm-metadata:start -->\n```json\n{\n  \"direct_parent\": null,\n  \"links\": [],\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"design\": null,\n    \"roadmap_item\": null,\n    \"priority\": null\n  },\n  \"pm_meta\": 1,\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"queue_id\": null,\n    \"scheduled_start\": null,\n    \"picked_up_at\": null,\n    \"work_started_at\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-23T23:48:24Z\",\n    \"session_id\": \"ses_e5df544f1f3ffe1Yyz8sGSOOYv\",\n    \"lane\": null,\n    \"host\": \"amd\",\n    \"worktree\": \"/home/user/git/code-wt-oc-code-07-2732\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"lane_start_issues\": [],\n    \"workspace_ref\": {\n      \"kind\": \"worktree\",\n      \"id\": \"/home/user/git/code-wt-oc-code-07-2732\",\n      \"repo\": \"developing-today/code\",\n      \"branch\": \"lane/oc-code-07-hard-stops-2732\",\n      \"sha\": \"13d9cffb88fa6b043667a3f052576663cbe1c206\"\n    },\n    \"auth_subject\": \"oc-code-04\",\n    \"stamped_by\": \"fleet 0.1.0 (native)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n<!-- pm-metadata:end -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1798069708&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=13866&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F13866&variant=start_proof&signature=e34db628e341493be891a7dddedc6f97d9e07fe136213ea6ba710fe2d427c9e9\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-start-proof-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-start-proof-v2-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Start