n39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/4547","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/4547","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/4547.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/4547.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-03T08:00:49Z"},"body":"Fixes #4069.\n\n## Problem\n`fold_authorisation` (pkgs/id/src/currency.rs) selected the live version with `max_by_key(version)` and no tie-break. Two issuer-signed bodies at the same highest version folded to different live rates depending on input order (Rust `max_by_key` returns the last equal element).\n\n## Fix\n- Highest-version selection now uses `max_by` on `(version, canonical body bytes)`: equal versions break ties by the lexicographically greatest canonical signed body bytes (`RateAuthorisation::body()`), independent of input order.\n- Fold doc comments (module + `fold_authorisation`) document the rule. Revoke tie-break semantics unchanged.\n- New regression test `same_version_authorisation_tie_break_is_input_order_independent`: same duplicate-version set in both orders folds to identical state.\n- Design decision recorded on #2290 (fold stays a fold over verified bodies alone; no event provenance widening).\n\nOut of scope (per packet): revoke tie-break, gateway #3801 / quote #3802, validation hardening #4071.\n\n## Tests\n- Red: new test FAILED against pre-fix code (reverse order folded Live 8000 vs expected Live 9000).\n- Green: `cargo test -p id --lib currency::` — 10/10 pass (9 existing + 1 new).\n\nQueue task 6306 · worker repo-worker-code · lane 02cafe76-eafd-4d0b-aaa6-2b7a737d68dc\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796239232&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=4547&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F4547&signature=8fcb3db15036bc9915d702e0fe42305c67bef71d2e361a269bed31889d1bee65\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/4547?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * When valid authorisations have the same version, selection now consistently favors the one with the lexicographically greatest canonical body, regardless of input order. This makes results deterministic when processing equal-version authorisations.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/4547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"